// ===================== 11.5 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('11.5  Which reader was this written for?'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open, and the second half is the one that matters: ⚠ **the pair kept from 11.3 — the student\'s own first version and the rewritten one — and the reader of the first.** **It is the approver in most cases, and it had been sent to an actor.** **Do not begin with somebody else\'s page**; the order of the stage is the whole of its usefulness.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** the approver _(passive, it has been agreed, in due course)_. **2** the actor _(imperative)_. **3** the record reader _(date, name, reason, past tense)_. ⚠ **4** **the writer** — _I have raised this three times and have had no reply_ — **which is true, important to the writer, and of no use to any of the three.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **count the imperatives and count the dates** — and Mr Hariri discovers a fourth reader nobody names: **the writer**, in a page that rehearses the writer\'s own difficulty, **with the history in the first paragraph.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **Do not rewrite it** — you have no standing to rewrite another office\'s notice and you will spend an afternoon on it. **Ask the one question the version you needed would have answered**: for an actor, six words — **_what do I do, and when?_**   **2** **The history in the first paragraph.** _Considered at some length · following consultation · I have raised this three times._'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The fourth reader is the finding of the cycle and it has to be named, because there is no ordinary phrase for it: the page written for the writer.** It is not vanity and it is not padding. **A writer who has been carrying a difficulty writes the difficulty down**, because the difficulty is the part they are holding — **and the page is perfectly honest and reaches nobody.** Mr Hariri\'s count is the example: **eight of his eleven pages, all eight opening on the history.** ⚠ **The repair is not to delete the history but to move it**, and the class should see both versions of the same sentence: _I have asked about this three times_ **in the first paragraph is a complaint**; _asked on 2 September, 14 November and 6 January; no reply to any_ **in the record paragraph is evidence.** **Same facts, two sentences, and only one of them gets anybody anything.**'));
