out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Lubna gave the order and the lengths: actor, approver, record — shortest first and longest last, and her survey note is forty words, ninety and a hundred and sixty. And the one line at the top, before the layers: the second survey runs on the 3rd, 4th and 5th of March — one sentence, what and when, and the only thing all three readers need. Which is the architecture of the whole unit in four lines: one summary, three layers, each layer headed with its reader named. A heading that names its reader is the cheapest device in the book, and in a long page it is worth more than any amount of good prose. Omar asked why the record layer is the longest when it seems the least urgent, and because it has to carry what nobody will remember: the actor will be in the room on the day and the approver will remember approving it for about a month, while the record reader has nothing but the page, so everything that was obvious at the time has to be written down. Lubna said it is the layer she writes last and resents writing, and everybody does, for a reason worth knowing — it is the only layer that does nothing for you now: the actor\'s layer gets the thing done, the approver\'s layer gets it allowed, and the record layer is a gift to somebody who may be your own successor. It is also the layer that, two years later, is the only one anybody thanks you for. Dima asked what the one thing never to do is, and it is to write a single paragraph that tries to serve two readers: the date stamp, which the directorate has approved and which adds about nine seconds, should be applied from Monday is an instruction with an approval inside it, and it is read by both and acted on by neither, because the actor hears a justification and the approver hears an order. Jad asked how long the whole page can be, and one side in working life and about three hundred words — longer and the actor stops at the heading of the second layer, which is the right thing for them to do and means the summary was not at the top. And Hiba asked what transfers to the examination, where the essay has one reader and four paragraphs: not the layering but the discipline — decide what each paragraph is for before you write it, because a paragraph with two jobs loses the organisation mark.']));
