out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report – mediation (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['One notice, three readers, four weeks, nothing done. Asked which reader it was written for, Omar said the approver — passive, it has been agreed, in due course. Then the test: count the imperatives and count the dates. No imperatives, no dates, and the first six words are the question of the second page, which is the writer telling us the question existed. It was written for the writer. Which is the finding of the cycle and the fourth kind of page: a page acted on by nobody has usually been written for the writer, and the tell is the history in the first paragraph — considered at some length, following consultation — neither of which is a fact about anything that is going to happen. Dima asked for the mediation, and it is three moves and not the moves of 10.7: ask each of the three readers what they did; name the reader the page was written for; and write the missing version for the other two. And that is the whole of it, because there is nothing to settle — there is no dispute. Jad asked whether there is no dispute at all, and none, which is what makes this the hardest kind to find: nobody disagreed with anybody, three readers each waited for one of the others, and nothing in the page told any of them that they were the one, so four weeks passed and no two people in it were ever in conflict. Mazen said and nobody complains because nobody knows, which is why this kind runs for months where a dispute runs for weeks: a quarrel has an end, because somebody wins or somebody gives up, and a page nobody acted on has no end at all — it simply stops being recent, and then it becomes the file\'s only record that anything was decided. Hiba asked what you write in place of it, and two versions and not three, because the writer\'s own already exists: the actor\'s is from 1 March give out the one-page form, and the two-page forms go in the second drawer and stay there; the approver\'s is I am asking you to confirm in writing that the second page is discontinued from 1 March. Nineteen words and twenty-one, and the four weeks would not have happened. Rim asked about the record version, and it is written now and dated now, saying what was found and when. And Lubna asked who is at fault, and the writer and only the writer, which is the one place this book names a fault: the three readers all behaved correctly, because each of them did the right thing with a page that asked nothing of them.']));
out.push(A('Listener task: the two missing versions from the student\'s own case and the reader the original was written for. ⚠ **Enforce the instruction about sending.** The repair goes out **as the notice and not as a correction**: a reader handed a correction **reads about the error**, and a reader handed an instruction **does the thing.** **The explanation belongs in the record paragraph**, where it is dated and where nobody has to read it to act. **About a third of the room will send an apology instead of an instruction**, and that is the last thing to catch in this book.'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**✗** Blaming the readers. → **✓** three readers behaved correctly; the fault is the writer\'s.   **✗** Sending the repair as a correction. → **✓** send it as the notice.   **✗** An undated record paragraph written late. → **✓** dated today, and saying it is late.   **✗** _In due course_ in the repair. → **✓** a date.   **✗** Calling Case B careless. → **✓** the missing clause of reason.'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read – exam practice (B2 First Reading and Use of English Part 2)'));
out.push(A('**1** at   **2** in   **3** because _(also: since · as)_   **4** but _(also: yet)_   **5** from   **6** for   **7** without   **8** that _(also: this)_'));
out.push(A('Three things to say about this task, because it is the first Part 2 of the course. ⚠ **Every answer in Part 2 is a grammar word — a preposition, a conjunction, an auxiliary, a pronoun, an article — and never a content word.** A candidate who writes a noun or a main verb has misread the part, **and that is the single commonest error in it.** ⚠ Items **1**, **5**, **6** and **7** are **dependent prepositions and fixed phrases**: _at all_, _tell from_, _for a reason_, _without anybody noticing_ — **and the words either side of the gap decide them**, so read both sides before writing. And items **3**, **4** and **8** admit alternatives: **accept any word that is grammatical and keeps the sense**, and teach candidates to write **the commonest word that fits** rather than the most interesting one.'));
