out.push(A('Items **1** and **4** are the bare infinitive after _please_ and after _shall_, which is where students who speak well write badly. **2**, **3** and **5** are the declared phrasal verbs in three different forms — **past simple, passive participle and separated object** — and **3** is the one to work through: _was flagged up_, where the participle and not the bare verb is needed after _was_. ⚠ Items **6**, **7** and **8** are the word-formation set: **ambiguity, instruction, response** — and **6** is wrong most often, **because the adjective sounds like a noun in that slot.**'));
out.push(S('Unit 11 check · B  Listening (B2 First Listening Part 3 style – multiple matching)'));
out.push(A('**Speaker 1** F   **Speaker 2** C   **Speaker 3** G   **Speaker 4** H   **Speaker 5** B   _(A, D and E are not used)_'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 3 is multiple matching and the difficulty is the three unused options**, which are written to be plausible for more than one speaker. **Option A** — _told me what to do but not when_ — is close to Speaker 1, who **was** told what to do; but his trouble was **where** and not when, so A is wrong and F is right. ⚠ **Option G** will tempt candidates on Speaker 2, who did nothing for nine days — **but G is about a missing fallback and Speaker 3 is the one with no fallback.** **Teach the one habit: read all eight options before the recording starts, and mark the two or three that could fit nobody.** Then the five that remain are a shorter list. **And play it twice**, as the examination does.'));
out.push(S('Unit 11 check · C  Writing'));
out.push(A('The essay, and marked on four things only: **four paragraphs with one job each; the concession paragraph third with the objection in its first sentence; all three notes answered; and the candidate\'s own idea in the last paragraph with nothing else in it.** ⚠ Nothing else is assessed. **A paragraph with two jobs is the fault this unit adds**, and it is the commonest way to lose the organisation mark in two hundred words — **and it is almost always the last paragraph, where the own idea arrives on top of the conclusion.**'));
out.push(S('I can… (Unit 11)'));
out.push(A('Self-assessment; no answers. The four that matter are the first, the third, the sixth and the seventh: **naming the three readers**, **an actor\'s version with no passive**, **naming the one risk myself**, and **naming which reader a page was written for by counting.** ⚠ A class that ticks the layering item and not those four **has learnt a page format and not a habit** — and the counting is the habit, **because it is the only one of the eight that can be done to somebody else\'s page in ten seconds.**'));
